WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.834 --> 00:00:05.340
Rig OS is a local computer-use runtime. This is a tour of its public architecture and documentation.

2
00:00:05.397 --> 00:00:09.602
Models propose actions. You review them. The runtime checks permission and current state before input.

3
00:00:09.766 --> 00:00:13.781
The system map connects 120 responsibilities. Each box leads to its explanation and source.

4
00:00:13.812 --> 00:00:17.115
Choose a journey to follow one workflow through the system, in order.

5
00:00:17.164 --> 00:00:20.174
Step through the handoffs. See which component owns each decision.

6
00:00:20.290 --> 00:00:23.097
Descriptions include the boundaries and limits of each responsibility.

7
00:00:23.176 --> 00:00:27.376
Open the exact source snapshot with the cited line highlighted.

8
00:00:27.507 --> 00:00:30.714
Search source paths when you already know where you want to look.

9
00:00:30.856 --> 00:00:34.260
The documentation library publishes all 51 Markdown documents from the repository.

10
00:00:35.307 --> 00:00:39.308
Search the full text. Read setup, architecture, operating guides, and recorded evidence.

11
00:00:39.331 --> 00:00:42.832
Read the document, copy commands, or go back to the original source.

12
00:00:43.363 --> 00:00:47.177
Keep the limits visible. Recorded results have a scope, and failed gates stay in the documentation.

13
00:00:47.699 --> 00:00:52.212
Explore at rig-os.netlify.app. Built by Brad Clonan, open to Software Architect, Staff / Principal Engineer, and applied AI roles.
